<section id="slcOutcomes" class="section-content section-margin article-text">
    <article class="gap-v gap-h">
        <h2>Outcomes and Lessons</h2>
        <p>The next primary step is to go through user testing with multiple participants for the Consumers’ side. I
            would also like to build out the Farmers’ side of the platform for where they can order compost, animal
            bedding and list what tickets are available.</p>
        <h3>Future Features</h3>
        <p>Assuming all goes well with the testing and subsequent iterations, here are some features I think should be
            added to Second Life:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>
                <p>The ability to take a photo of their receipt and add the food to a digital “fridge” to let you know
                    when your food is about to turn.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>With the digital “fridge”, Second Life will be able to recommend recipes based on what you have (and
                    tell you what you may need to buy).</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Ability to connect with local food pantries, community fridges, and other local organizations to see
                    what they may need, and how you can help them.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </article>
</section>